        "worked_solution": "The formula for ${}_{n}{P}_{r}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{P}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=40$ and $r=3$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{40}{P}_{3} & =\\frac{40!}{(40-3)!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40!}{37!} \\\\  & =\\frac{40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38\\cdot \\cancel{37!}}{\\cancel{37!}} \\\\  & =40\\cdot 39\\cdot 38 \\\\  & =59\\,280.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
